From 8616f22d31d2ffbd1a7a25b95328c52e8799e786 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tillmann Severin <tillmann.severin@mailbox.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:32:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/fb-helper: reject a change of the visible resolution

drm_fb_helper_set_par() does not look at the variable screen info at
all, it only restores the mode the fbdev client has configured. A
request for a different visible resolution is therefore acknowledged
without ever reaching the screen, and user space is left believing it
drives a smaller display than the one being scanned out.

Applications that size their drawing from the returned resolution then
work on a geometry that does not exist, which places their output at
the wrong offset.

The comment above the existing test already states that settings which
are not pushed back to KMS have to fail, but the test only catches a
resolution that does not fit the framebuffer. Reject a differing
visible resolution as well.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c
index f1bb87f27dd1..0e9ff0d7857a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_fb_helper.c
@@ -1271,6 +1271,19 @@ int drm_fb_helper_check_var(struct fb_var_screeninfo *var,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * fb_set_par() cannot change the display mode, so a request for a
+	 * different visible resolution would be acknowledged without ever
+	 * reaching the screen. Reject it rather than leave user space with a
+	 * framebuffer whose geometry does not match what is scanned out.
+	 */
+	if (var->xres != info->var.xres || var->yres != info->var.yres) {
+		drm_dbg_kms(dev, "fbdev emulation doesn't support changing the resolution, "
+			    "request %dx%d != %dx%d\n",
+			    var->xres, var->yres, info->var.xres, info->var.yres);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	__fill_var(var, info, fb);
 
 	/*
